{
	"gauge": "<div class=\"gauge wide\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 200,000-token context window drawn to scale. Claude Code compacts at 167,000 tokens, Codex at 180,000 and pi at 183,616.\">\n  <div class=\"bar\"><div class=\"fill\"></div><i class=\"tk cc\"></i><i class=\"tk cx\"></i><i class=\"tk pi\"></i></div>\n  <div class=\"ends\"><span>0</span><span>200,000 tokens</span></div>\n  <div class=\"keys\"><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-cc)\">Claude Code compacts at <b>167,000</b></span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-cx)\">Codex at <b>180,000</b></span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-pi)\">pi at <b>183,616</b></span></div>\n</div>",
	"creeds": "<div class=\"creeds wide\">\n  <div class=\"cx\"><h3>Codex</h3><p class=\"creed\">Trusts the server</p><p>It sends no separate system prompt. On OpenAI's own models, compaction happens server-side and comes back as an encrypted item the client can't read. Locally, it keeps the user's own words and summarizes the rest.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"cc\"><h3>Claude Code</h3><p class=\"creed\">Trusts the disk</p><p>Oversized output is saved to a file and replaced by a preview. After a compaction it reads files again instead of remembering old tool results. After a long idle it clears old results outright. It has the most layers.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"pi\"><h3>pi</h3><p class=\"creed\">Trusts the conversation</p><p>It keeps the last 20,000 tokens as they were, tool results included, and edits its summary in place instead of rewriting it. Nearly everything else is left to extensions.</p></div>\n</div>",
	"f-race": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-race\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 1</b>The same session through three harnesses</span><span id=\"race-step\">step 0</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"race-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"race-w\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Context window\"><button data-v=\"200000\" aria-pressed=\"true\">200K window</button><button data-v=\"272000\">272K</button><button data-v=\"1000000\">1M</button></div>\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"race-play\">Pause</button>\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"race-reset\">Restart</button>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>One synthetic session (user turns, model replies, tool calls and their results) is fed to all three. Each bar is one harness's context. The tick on each bar is where that harness compacts, using its real trigger rule. After a compaction each bar drops to what that harness keeps. The trigger rules are exact; the session and the sizes after compaction are illustrative <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-trig": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-trig\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 2</b>Trigger arithmetic</span><span>exact formulas</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"trig-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"trig-w\">Context window</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"trig-w\" min=\"0\" max=\"5\" step=\"1\" value=\"1\"><output id=\"trig-w-out\"></output></div>\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"trig-o\">Claude Code max output</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"trig-o\" min=\"4\" max=\"64\" step=\"4\" value=\"32\"><output id=\"trig-o-out\"></output></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"trig-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>Drag the window size and watch the three rules diverge. Claude Code's max-output deduction only changes anything below 20K, because it is capped there. Codex's configured limit can only move its trigger down; the 90% cap always applies.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-req": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-req\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 3</b>Request layout and the cache line</span><span id=\"req-ev\">initial request</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"req-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"req-btns\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Event\">\n      <button data-e=\"mcp\">MCP server connects</button><button data-e=\"load\">Model loads a tool</button><button data-e=\"compact\">Compaction</button><button data-e=\"clear\">Old results cleared</button><button data-e=\"model\">Switch model</button>\n    </div>\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"req-reset\">Reset</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"req-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>Hover or tap a block for details. Each column is one request, top to bottom in wire order. Green is read from cache, orange is written to cache (or reprocessed), and the dashed line marks the first changed byte. Block heights are proportional to tokens <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>; the placement of each event is from source or binary.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-trunc": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-trunc\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 4</b>What the model receives from a long output</span><span id=\"trunc-size\"></span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"trunc-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"trunc-n\">Output size</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"trunc-n\" min=\"0\" max=\"8\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\"><output id=\"trunc-n-out\"></output></div>\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"trunc-pos\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Error position\"><button data-v=\"0.03\">Error near start</button><button data-v=\"0.5\" aria-pressed=\"true\">in the middle</button><button data-v=\"0.985\">near end</button></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"three\">\n    <div class=\"pane cx\"><h4>Codex <span class=\"badge\" id=\"tr-cx-b\"></span></h4><div class=\"meta\" id=\"tr-cx-m\"></div><pre class=\"term\" id=\"tr-cx\"></pre></div>\n    <div class=\"pane cc\"><h4>Claude Code <span class=\"badge\" id=\"tr-cc-b\"></span></h4><div class=\"meta\" id=\"tr-cc-m\"></div><pre class=\"term\" id=\"tr-cc\"></pre></div>\n    <div class=\"pane pi\"><h4>pi <span class=\"badge\" id=\"tr-pi-b\"></span></h4><div class=\"meta\" id=\"tr-pi-m\"></div><pre class=\"term\" id=\"tr-pi\"></pre></div>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>The strips show the full output top to bottom, with the part each harness passes to the model highlighted and the error line in red. The panes show the start and end of what the model actually receives (long middles collapsed for display). The log is generated; the cut rules are the shipped defaults, slightly simplified: Codex's 1.2× serialization allowance and its exact header format are omitted.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-compact": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-compact\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 5</b>One compaction, three outcomes</span><span id=\"cmp-state\">before</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"cmp-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <button class=\"btn primary\" id=\"cmp-go\">Compact</button>\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"cmp-back\">Reset</button>\n    <label class=\"toggle\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"cmp-remote\"> Codex on an OpenAI provider (server-side compaction)</label>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"legend\">\n    <span style=\"--sw:var(--td-sys)\">system / instructions</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-mem)\">memory files</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-user)\">user</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-asst)\">assistant</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-call)\">tool call</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-res)\">tool result</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-sum)\">summary</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"cmp-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>Hover or tap a block for details. The same history (left to right, oldest first) compacted by each harness's rules. Blocks that survive verbatim slide to their new position; everything else folds into the summary. Block sizes are illustrative <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>. What survives, and the order for Codex local, Claude Code and pi, is from source and binary; the layout of Codex's remote result is simplified.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-probe": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-probe\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 6</b>Recall after a compaction</span><span>derived from the rules, not measured</span></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\" style=\"margin-top:0\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"probe-age\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"How old is the detail\"><button data-v=\"tail\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Detail is recent (last ~20K tokens)</button><button data-v=\"mid\">Earlier in the session</button><button data-v=\"old\">Before a previous compaction</button></div>\n    <label class=\"toggle\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"probe-remote\"> Codex on an OpenAI provider</label>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"probe\" id=\"probe-grid\"></div>\n  <div class=\"legend\" id=\"probe-legend\"></div>\n  <figcaption>\"Summary only\" means the answer survives only if the summarizer chose to write it down, in its own words. \"Gone\" means the model would have to run a tool again, or can't recover it at all. Codex's server-side compaction returns an encrypted item, so what it retains can't be inspected.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"prompts": "<div class=\"cards wide\">\n  <div class=\"card cx\"><h4>Codex</h4><div class=\"src\">prompts/templates/compact/prompt.md</div>\n    <blockquote>\"You are performing a CONTEXT CHECKPOINT COMPACTION. Create a handoff summary for another LLM that will resume the task.\"</blockquote>\n    <ol><li>Current progress and key decisions</li><li>Context, constraints, preferences</li><li>What remains (next steps)</li><li>Critical data, examples, references</li></ol>\n    The summary is then prefixed with \"Another language model started to solve this problem and produced a summary of its thinking process…\"</div>\n  <div class=\"card cc\"><h4>Claude Code</h4><div class=\"src\">binary strings, 2.1.317</div>\n    <blockquote>\"Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far, paying close attention to the user's explicit requests and your previous actions.\"</blockquote>\n    <ol><li>Primary Request and Intent</li><li>Key Technical Concepts</li><li>Files and Code Sections</li><li>Errors and fixes</li><li>Problem Solving</li><li>All user messages</li><li>Pending Tasks</li><li>Current Work</li><li>Optional Next Step</li></ol>\n    Written as an <code>&lt;analysis&gt;</code> pass, then the <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code>. One variant caps it at 2,000 words.</div>\n  <div class=\"card pi\"><h4>pi</h4><div class=\"src\">packages/coding-agent/src/core/compaction/compaction.ts</div>\n    <blockquote>\"Create a structured context checkpoint summary that another LLM will use to continue the work. Use this EXACT format:\"</blockquote>\n    <ol><li>Goal</li><li>Constraints &amp; Preferences</li><li>Progress: Done / In Progress / Blocked</li><li>Key Decisions</li><li>Next Steps</li><li>Critical Context</li></ol>\n    On the second compaction it switches to an update prompt: \"PRESERVE all existing information… move items from 'In Progress' to 'Done'\".</div>\n</div>",
	"f-sumin": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-sumin\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 7</b>Tokens the summarizer reads</span><span>80 tool calls</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"sumin-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"legend\"><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-user)\">user</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-asst)\">assistant</span><span style=\"--sw:color-mix(in srgb, var(--td-asst) 45%, transparent)\">thinking</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-call)\">tool calls</span><span style=\"--sw:var(--td-res)\">tool results</span></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"sumin-r\">Average tool result</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"sumin-r\" min=\"0\" max=\"7\" step=\"1\" value=\"4\"><output id=\"sumin-r-out\"></output></div>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>A session with 80 tool calls, recomposed as the average result size changes. pi's 2,000-character cap per result (about 500 tokens) bounds what its summarizer reads no matter how chatty the tools are. Codex's remote path is shown separately because the input is processed server-side. Proportions are illustrative <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-idle": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-idle\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 8</b>What happens while you're away</span><span>pi's real warming formula</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"idle-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"idle-t\">Time away</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"idle-t\" min=\"1\" max=\"120\" step=\"1\" value=\"70\"><output id=\"idle-t-out\"></output></div>\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"idle-c\">Context size</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"idle-c\" min=\"0\" max=\"9\" step=\"1\" value=\"4\"><output id=\"idle-c-out\"></output></div>\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"idle-ttl\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Cache lifetime\"><button data-v=\"5\" aria-pressed=\"true\">5-min cache</button><button data-v=\"60\">1-hour cache</button></div>\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"idle-price\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Price tier\"><button data-v=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"true\">$3/M input</button><button data-v=\"5\">$5/M</button><button data-v=\"15\">$15/M</button></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"idle-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>pi's decision uses its shipped formula: expected saving = 0.15 × (write cost − read cost) − cost of one refresh. Prices use Anthropic's ratios: reads at 0.1×, writes at 1.25× (5-minute) or 2× (1-hour) of the input price. Claude Code's cleared amount assumes 45% of context is old tool results <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-sub": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-sub\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 9</b>What a child inherits</span><span id=\"sub-mode\"></span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"sub-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"sub-btns\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Spawn mode\">\n      <button data-m=\"cxnew\">Codex spawn</button><button data-m=\"cxfork\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Codex fork</button><button data-m=\"cxpre\">Codex fork, keep prefix</button><button data-m=\"ccsub\">Claude Code subagent</button><button data-m=\"ccfork\">Claude Code fork</button><button data-m=\"pi\">pi extension</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"sub-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>Hover or tap a block for details. The parent's history (top) is copied into the child's window (bottom) under each mode's filter. Faded blocks are dropped. Sizes are illustrative <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>; the filters are from source and documentation.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-disk": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-disk\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 10</b>Resuming a session</span><span id=\"disk-state\">press Resume</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"disk-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <button class=\"btn primary\" id=\"disk-go\">Resume</button>\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"disk-reset\">Reset</button>\n  </div>\n  <figcaption>Each column is a session file, oldest line at the top. Resume scans from the end back to the latest compaction record, then rebuilds context from there. pi's file is a tree: lines point to a parent, and only the branch leading to the current leaf counts.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
	"f-all": "<figure class=\"fig\" id=\"f-all\">\n  <div class=\"tag\"><span><b>Fig. 11</b>One session, every rule</span><span>same model and prices for all three</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stage\" id=\"all-canvas\"></div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"all-preset\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Session type\"><button data-v=\"tools\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Noisy tools (test logs, builds)</button><button data-v=\"talk\">Mostly conversation</button><button data-v=\"reads\">Many medium-sized outputs</button></div>\n    <div class=\"ctl\"><label for=\"all-n\">Length</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"all-n\" min=\"100\" max=\"600\" step=\"20\" value=\"300\"><output id=\"all-n-out\"></output></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"readout\" id=\"all-read\"></div>\n  <figcaption>Each step is a model turn with one shell command; the raw output sizes are drawn from the chosen session type. Output caps, compaction triggers and what each harness keeps afterwards follow the rules above; the kept sizes and the session itself are illustrative <span class=\"td-ev\">model</span>. Cost assumes $3 per million input tokens, cache reads at 0.1×, cache writes at 1.25×, and counts each compaction's summarizer call. Dashed lines are the three triggers.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
}